\f2\b  Project Architecture\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 A modern F1 dashboard shouldn't request data from FastF1 every time a user refreshes the page\'97it\'92s too slow. Instead, use an 
\f2\b Asynchronous Worker
\f1\b0  pattern.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls10\ilvl0
\f2\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 The UI:
\f1\b0  React requests data for "Session X".\
\ls10\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 The API:
\f1\b0  Checks 
\f2\b Redis
\f1\b0 . If data is there, it returns in milliseconds.\
\ls10\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 The Worker:
\f1\b0  If data is missing, a background task (using 
\f2\b Celery
\f1\b0  or 
\f2\b AWS Lambda
\f1\b0 ) triggers FastF1 to download, process, and cache the session.\
\ls10\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 The Storage:
\f1\b0  Raw FastF1 cache files should be stored in 
\f2\b Amazon S3
\f1\b0  to prevent re-downloads across different server restarts.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
