\f2\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec5 3. System Architecture\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The architecture follows a 
\f2\b Producer-Consumer
\f1\b0  pattern to prevent the Python processing from slowing down the UI.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls15\ilvl0
\f2\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Ingestion Layer:
\f1\b0  FastAPI fetches data from FastF1, processes it into "UI-ready" JSON (e.g., converting raw (x,y)coordinates into SVG paths), and stores it in Redis.\
\ls15\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 API Layer:
\f1\b0  A REST or WebSocket API serves the processed data to the frontend.\
\ls15\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec5 Client Layer:
\f1\b0  The Next.js frontend consumes the data. It uses a 
\f2\b Global Timeline Controller
\f1\b0  to sync all modules (e.g., if you scrub to Lap 20, the Tyre and Strategy modules update simultaneously).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \strokec6 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

